# Generated from: specs/bug-prevent-spec-only-publication-from-closing-umbrella-issues/requirements.md
# Issue: #161
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @issue-161 @write-spec @github
Feature: Spec-only umbrella publication is non-closing
  Spec-only publication previously reused the issue-linked sealing branch and trusted
  non-closing body wording, allowing GitHub to close an umbrella before child delivery.
  Publication must use an unlinked branch and verify actual closing and timeline state.

  @regression
  Scenario: Publish an umbrella specification without a closing relationship
    Given an open umbrella has incomplete child work and an issue-linked sealing branch
    When write-spec publishes the exact seal commit through its dedicated unlinked publication branch
    Then the pull request head is the expected unlinked publication ref
    And closingIssuesReferences does not contain the umbrella
    And the workflow reports publication_pending only after that semantic proof

  @regression
  Scenario: Keep the umbrella open after a safe publication merge
    Given an exact marked specification-only publication pull request is pending-safe
    When the pull request merges and the canonical default-branch tree is refreshed
    Then the umbrella issue remains open while required children are incomplete
    And no ClosedEvent tied to the publication pull request exists
    And child transition proceeds only after both Git and GitHub proofs pass

  @regression
  Scenario: Detect a publication pull request that closes its umbrella
    Given GitHub lists the umbrella in a marked publication pull request's closingIssuesReferences
    When write-spec classifies the publication before or after merge
    Then it reports a lifecycle error with exact issue, pull-request, branch, marker, and timeline evidence
    And it does not report publication_pending or successful coordination state

  @regression
  Scenario: Recover only an umbrella closed by its exact marked publication
    Given the exact marked specification-only publication pull request merged
    And the umbrella's currently active closure is a ClosedEvent whose repository-qualified closer is that pull request
    When the operator invokes the supported recovery and explicitly approves reopening that exact issue
    Then the workflow reopens only that umbrella
    And it refetches the issue and requires it to be open before continuing
    And an unrelated or unverifiable closure is never reopened through this path
    And a historical publication closure cleared by reopen cannot override a later unrelated closure

  @regression
  Scenario: Preserve intentional closure for ordinary implementation delivery
    Given a non-umbrella implementation issue is delivered through the ordinary open-pr workflow
    When its pull request intentionally closes the issue at merge
    Then the existing issue-closing contract remains available and correctly represented
    And no Seal-Spec publication branch or umbrella recovery rule is applied

  @regression
  Scenario: Preserve exact publication scope and branch safety
    Given the approved umbrella spec has a validated seal commit and source tree
    When write-spec prepares its dedicated publication branch and pull request
    Then the publication ref resolves to the exact full seal commit
    And only the approved spec directory differs from the default branch
    And no version, changelog, manifest, marketplace, unrelated path, force-push, or issue-linked publication branch is used

  @regression
  Scenario: Exercise actual linked and unlinked GitHub closing semantics
    Given an explicitly configured disposable GitHub repository
    When the live exercise creates and merges an issue-linked specification-only control pull request and an unlinked publication pull request
    Then the control records its actual closingIssuesReferences and ClosedEvent timeline outcome
    And the unlinked publication excludes its umbrella from closingIssuesReferences
    And the unlinked umbrella remains open after merge with no publication-linked ClosedEvent
